```ts
export interface Entry {
  readonly id: string;
  readonly weight: number;
}

export class EntryBook {
  add(entry: Entry): void;
  remove(id: string): boolean;
  select(id: string): boolean;
  move(offset: number): Entry | null;
  current(): Entry | null;
  list(): Entry[];
}
```

The book preserves insertion order. `add` rejects blank IDs and non-finite weights with `RangeError`. Entries must be copied when stored. Adding an existing ID replaces its value without changing its position or selection. `remove` returns false for an unknown ID. If the selected entry is removed, select the entry now occupying the removed index, wrapping to the first entry when necessary; an empty book has no selection. `select` returns false for an unknown ID. `move` requires an integer offset, otherwise throwing `RangeError`. On a nonempty book, it moves from the selected entry with circular wrapping; when nothing is selected, offset zero starts at the first entry, positive offsets count forward from it, and negative offsets count backward from it. `current` and `list` return fresh objects so callers cannot mutate stored state. Ordering must remain deterministic.

